WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.400
Module 10 · Course 4 · Protect · For entrepreneurs
Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.800
Build your legal and compliance framework before you launch: know your duties, write the policies you need, manage risk.

3
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:30.985
This module helps you build your legal and compliance framework before you launch: a map of your duties, the policies you need, contract checks, usable procedures, safe ways to raise concerns and a risk register. It answers: what could go wrong?

4
00:00:31.385 --> 00:00:31.985
Why protect before you launch

5
00:00:31.985 --> 00:00:38.030
1. Safeguarding and data protection apply from your very first activity or sign-up.

6
00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:44.074
2. A few policies people actually follow beat a pile of copied documents.

7
00:00:44.074 --> 00:00:51.489
3. Contracts arrive before you are fully set up; checks protect you from surprises.

8
00:00:51.889 --> 00:01:03.389
What you will work through: 10.1 Your legal and regulatory map · 10.2 Working out which policies you actually need · 10.3 Contracts and agreements · 10.4 Core policies: conduct, conflicts and anti-fraud · 10.5 Safeguarding · 10.6 Data protection and privacy · 10.7 Whistleblowing, complaints and incident reporting · 10.8 HR and workplace policies · 10.9 Writing usable procedures · 10.10 Policy management and review · 10.11 Identifying and assessing risk · 10.12 Risk registers, ownership, mitigation and escalation · 10.13 Monitoring and reviewing risk · 10.14 Recap: Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk

9
00:01:03.789 --> 00:01:04.389
What you will have

10
00:01:04.389 --> 00:01:10.804
1. A legal map of the duties linked to your form, activities and location.

11
00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:16.848
2. Core policies with usable procedures and a safe route to raise concerns.

12
00:01:16.848 --> 00:01:23.522
3. A short risk register with owners, actions and early warning signs.

13
00:01:23.922 --> 00:01:24.522
Practical tips

14
00:01:24.522 --> 00:01:30.196
1. Check local rules with someone with a legal background before registering.

15
00:01:30.196 --> 00:01:36.611
2. Write procedures for what you do today, even if only you do it.

16
00:01:36.611 --> 00:01:43.656
3. Our example bakery shows why safeguarding matters when some trainees are 17.

17
00:01:44.256 --> 00:01:46.256
You create: Your Compliance & Risk Pack: legal map, policies, procedures and risk register.

18
00:01:46.256 --> 00:01:51.056
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

19
00:01:52.556 --> 00:01:55.656
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
